  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Data driven aquaculture capacity building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A new project that aims to improve the technical and economic performance of Tanzanian fish farmers, has been launched. The project will develop a training tool based on accurate data on fish farm performance in Tanzania. Aquaculture trainers often lack knowledge of the issues that Tanzanian farmers face and rely on outdated, inaccurate, or international farm conditions when designing courses. The new training tool and method will be developed based on data collected from representative farmers. This practical approach will ensure that the tool is tailored to the needs of Tanzanian fish farmers. The tools and knowledge gained from the project will be made available to the wider sector and students.</narrative>
  </description>
